From: Nuvoton OpenBMC <noreply@nuvoton.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spdmd: publish "authenticating" association for ComponentIntegrity

bmcweb's Redfish ComponentIntegrity resource (added by this distro's
meta-evb-npcm845 bmcweb patches) resolves TargetComponentURI by reading
the D-Bus association named "authenticating" off each
xyz.openbmc_project.Attestation.ComponentIntegrity object
(redfish-core/lib/component_integrity.hpp: afterGetComponentTarget()
queries "<objectPath>/authenticating"). Without it, the ObjectMapper has
no such association object and bmcweb's GetAssociatedSubTreePaths call
fails with EBADR ("Invalid request descriptor"), which bmcweb reports as
an internal error on every GET of /redfish/v1/ComponentIntegrity/{id}.

NVIDIA's Responder::Responder only ever publishes "transport_object" and
"inventory_object" associations, which bmcweb never looks for, so the
target link was never populated for any board using this fork.

Publish an additional "authenticating" association pointing at the same
invPath already passed to the constructor, so bmcweb can map it to a
Board/Chassis/Cpu/Dimm/PCIeDevice inventory interface as documented.
Guard on invPath actually being known (its filename is non-empty):
under this distro's -Ddiscovery_only_from_mctp_control=enabled build,
invPath is intentionally left empty when no Inventory.Item.SPDMResponder
match exists, and publishing an association to a bogus/root path would
just trade one confusing bmcweb error for another. In that case
ComponentIntegrity's target association legitimately doesn't exist yet
until this board's SPDM endpoints are given a real inventory path
(follow-up work, tracked separately).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [layer-local: bridges an out-of-tree
fork's D-Bus association naming to this distro's own bmcweb
ComponentIntegrity patches; not applicable upstream]

diff -ruN spdm-orig/spdmd/dbus_impl_responder.cpp spdm-fixed/spdmd/dbus_impl_responder.cpp
--- a/spdmd/dbus_impl_responder.cpp	2026-09-17 23:43:00.000000000 +0800
+++ b/spdmd/dbus_impl_responder.cpp	2026-09-17 23:44:00.000000000 +0800
@@ -70,6 +70,20 @@
                           mctpPath);
         prop.emplace_back("inventory_object", "spdm_responder_object", invPath);

+        // bmcweb's Redfish ComponentIntegrity resource (see the
+        // meta-evb-npcm845 bmcweb patches) resolves TargetComponentURI by
+        // reading the "authenticating" association off this object. Publish
+        // it whenever a real inventory object is known; upstream only
+        // publishes "inventory_object"/"transport_object", which nothing in
+        // bmcweb looks for, so ComponentIntegrity's target link was never
+        // populated. Skip it when invPath is empty (e.g. this distro's
+        // discovery_only_from_mctp_control build) rather than pointing the
+        // association at a bogus path.
+        if (!invPath.filename().empty())
+        {
+            prop.emplace_back("authenticating", "authenticated_by", invPath);
+        }
+
         associations(std::move(prop));
     }
     connection.registerTransport(transport);
